+{"created_at": "2026-06-29T14:05:22.295670+00:00", "ocr_backend": "sglang", "ocr_endpoint_version": "modal-sglang-unlimited-ocr-v1", "ocr_model": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_model_version": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_text": "<PAGE><|det|>title [112, 94, 471, 126]<|/det|>2. The Methodology\n<|det|>text [112, 170, 884, 214]<|/det|>Hemi Labs engaged CredShields to perform a VUSD Smart Contract audit. The following sections cover how the engagement was put together and executed.\n<|det|>title [113, 257, 336, 276]<|/det|>2.1 Preparation Phase\n<|det|>text [112, 316, 885, 459]<|/det|>The CredShields team meticulously reviewed all provided documents and comments in the smart contract code to gain a thorough understanding of the contract's features and functionalities. They meticulously examined all functions and created a mind map to systematically identify potential security vulnerabilities, prioritizing those that were more critical and business-sensitive for the refactored code. To confirm their findings, the team deployed a self-hosted version of the smart contract and performed verifications and validations during the audit phase.\n<|det|>text [112, 492, 884, 534]<|/det|>A testing window from March 4th, 2025, to March 7th, 2025, was agreed upon during the preparation phase.\n<|det|>title [113, 591, 228, 610]<|/det|>2.1.1 Scope\n<|det|>text [113, 625, 799, 642]<|/det|>During the preparation phase, the following scope for the engagement was agreed upon:\n<|det|>title [131, 658, 279, 674]<|/det|>IN SCOPE ASSETS\n<|det|>text [130, 687, 879, 721]<|/det|>https://github.com/hemilabs/vusd-stablecoin/tree/54f9f235f26df813152b3d3235e7f4373ce473b8\n<|det|>title [113, 777, 321, 795]<|/det|>2.1.2 Documentation\n<|det|>text [112, 814, 848, 831]<|/det|>Documentation was not required as the code was self-sufficient for understanding the project.\n<|det|>footer [909, 902, 971, 950]<|/det|>[Non-Text]\n", "page_image_sha256": "5362d6550991d004dba89bf522a258087aff9b2d1af058ed6ee673f42ec7239c", "pa